## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical batch ingestion, per-record contracts, privacy masking, and idempotent upserts in a common lakehouse pattern.

## Key Concepts

- Data contracts, masking, bad_data routing
- Iceberg schema evolution, upserts, unique keys
- Test plans for duplicates, new fields, and schema drift

## Code Example

```javascript
function validate(record) {
  const required = ["user_id","event_ts","event_type"];
  for (const k of required) if (!(k in record)) return false;
  // simple mask
  if (record.payload) record.payload.pii = null;
  return true;
}
```

```javascript
// MERGE-like upsert (pseudocode)
MERGE INTO iceberg.fact AS t
USING staging AS s
ON t.user_id = s.user_id AND t.event_ts = s.event_ts
WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET ...
WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT ...
```

## Why This Is Asked
Design a scalable, auditable CDC ingestion that evolves schemas safely while preserving privacy and lineage.

## Key Concepts
- Central schema registry with versioned contracts
- Idempotent upserts and MERGE semantics
- Dynamic schema evolution and tenant isolation
- Late data buffering and privacy-preserving BI views
- End-to-end testing and monitoring of contracts and lineage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: contract validation and upsert
function upsertEvent(event, registry) {
  const contract = registry.getContract(event.version, event.schemaKey);
  if (!contract.validate(event)) throw new Error('Contract violation');
  // perform idempotent merge into Iceberg
  mergeIntoIceberg(event, contract.primaryKey);
}
```

